<concept id="t00269">
	<title id="e01913">Outside temperature gauge</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>instrument cluster 
					<indexterm>outside temperature gauge</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>outside temperature gauge</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01914">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01915">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV035109.eps" align="center" placement="break" id="e01916"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>This gauge indicates the current outside air temperatures by 1°C (1°F).</p>
		<ul id="e01917">
			<li>
				<p>Temperature range: -40-60°C (-40-140°F)</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>The outside temperature on the display may not change immediately like a general thermometer to prevent the driver from being inattentive.</p>
		<p>To change the temperature unit (from °C to °F or from °F to °C)</p>
	</conbody>
</concept>